  "id": "Compound::DB00495 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Zidovudine, a nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor, is shown to bind to Slc22a11, which is involved in the transport of organic anions. This binding is further linked to the participation of Slc22a11 in sodium-independent organic anion transmembrane transport and inorganic anion exchanger activities, all of which are mediated by Slc22a6. The cumulative evidence suggests that Zidovudine may influence Slc22a6 through its interaction with Slc22a11, which is a key player in anion transport across cellular membranes. The mechanism involves Zidovudine potentially modulating the activity of Slc22a6 by affecting the transport function of Slc22a11, which could have implications for drug metabolism and transport in the body. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Zidovudine in altering the function of Slc22a6, though the exact nature of this interaction requires further experimental validation.",
